186231007} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2698090-661b-55d2-83a8-6279e0fb7d71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186231003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eea0f3ea-2e34-5271-8f21-b8a3054b7452" :question/math-academy-id "q-355207" :question/problem "Let $T=\\{-2,-1,0,1\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\ng(-2)=3,\\,g(-1)=-2,\\,g(0)=0,\\,g(1)=-2.\n$$\n\nCompute ${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x).$\n\n$\\,$\n${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${min}_{x\\in T}f(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}f(x)$ is an input in $T$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $3,$ $-2,$ $0,$ and $-2,$ so the minimum output value is $-2.$ This minimum occurs at both $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-2\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=\\{-1,1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f56e312-a8c4-5c65-9893-3ebc38120b4d" :knowledge-point/title "Distinguishing Between Max/Min and Argmax/Argmin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc9552db-fabc-56c1-84f8-b62c633ab799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc9552db-fabc-56c1-84f8-b62c633ab799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533681} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe9032c-6f44-58dc-9ddc-fa3ca07c4b0d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type