#uuid "6f68d534-8f10-5941-a10d-ac65abf5c7b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-355267" :question/problem "Let $S=\\{2,4,6,8\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\ng(2)=5,\\,g(4)=-3,\\,g(6)=10,\\,g(8)=0.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in S}g(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in S}g(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}g(x)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}g(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}g(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}g(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}g(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nHere, the outputs are $5,-3,10,$ and $0.$ \n\n- The largest output is $10,$ and it occurs at $x=6.$\n\n- The smallest output is $-3,$ and it occurs at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}g(x) & =10 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}g(x) & =6 \\\\ {min}_{x\\in S}g(x) & =-3 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}g(x) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f56e312-a8c4-5c65-9893-3ebc38120b4d" :knowledge-point/title "Distinguishing Between Max/Min and Argmax/Argmin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8796a66-f435-5714-9bbb-c1cb237fd64f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8796a66-f435-5714-9bbb-c1cb237fd64f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533668} :answer-field/id #uuid "081ebd9b-ca0f-5b1c-89d9-c6f0062cfe66" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218