ion.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70f30638-2aaa-5352-bc26-9df3570b67f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-355268" :question/problem "Let $S=\\{-2,0,1,4\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\nh(-2)=3,\\,h(0)=7,\\,h(1)=-5,\\,h(4)=2.\n$$\n\nCompute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the largest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that largest output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nHere, the outputs are $3,7,-5,$ and $2.$ \n\n- The largest output is $7,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$\n\n- The smallest output is $-5,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}h(x) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231451 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "258ff70f-5f41-5ea6-a0c2-bf74e7ce1cff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Argmax and Argmin With Ties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6509b98d-2629-5a0a-9c3c-d49a4074e5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533373} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b69ad2-29e6-5a20-847e-967b09441245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533565} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f25b4e-6dba-5c37-a869-7bf51a994ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ